  "claim": "For every nullable signed integer subject and every finite list of nullable signed integer alternatives, the source SQL three-valued IN fold equals typed-array ANY. The NOT IN fold equals the three-valued negation of that same ANY.",
  "assumptions": [
    "The verified PHP integer roles encode nullable mathematical integers and their exact resolved field coordinates. int4-to-int8 widening preserves the mathematical integer.",
    "The checked emitter writes all alternatives once in their stored order, casts their array to the stock signed int8 array, uses pg_catalog signed equality, and applies outer SQL NOT exactly for the negated case.",
    "The pinned PostgreSQL engines implement the stock SQL IN, NOT IN, array ANY, and logical operators according to the fixed semantic definitions. Source resolution must select the stock profile. The native schedule tests this premise separately.",
    "All operands belong to the pure signed leaf domain, so source operator evaluation order and representation changes leave the observed equality result and effects intact."
  ],
